  "date": "mid 1950s",
  "content": "At the age of 7 or 8, I underwent a tonsillectomy under general anesthetic. I recall the mask being applied to my face. I was then aware of traveling through a dark tunnel. I found myself on a road winding down to a beautiful rural place, which contained a large rustic house set in a valley with a forest behind it. There was a sparkling river and the meadows in front of it were golden and peaceful. There may have been a mill wheel at the far side of the house, through which a stream flowed. The forest behind, looked safe and inviting and I was curious to see it and remain there. At some point, I found myself turned around on the road facing up towards where the tunnel had ended. I remember nothing beyond this point.",
